  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_003 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat) at 0.4348 acc, with RNA clearly dominant (rna_only 0.4106 vs image_only 0.2266) and concat slightly beating weighted fusion. The profile/aggregation axis is completely untested. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve performance while keeping the same encoders (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l) and the same fusion (concat)? Why this is the best next step: config_009 is the most direct, minimal extension of the current best config—only profile_setting and aggregation change, isolating the effect of multiprofile + aggregation. Using avgpool (rather than transformer) is a conservative first probe of this axis; if it helps, a follow-up with transformer aggregation becomes a clean comparison. This is more informative than jumping to a new encoder or a more complex aggregation, as it reduces uncertainty about whether the profile dimension matters at all before investing in more complex variants."
}

